    affiliation: "Department of Biomechanics, University of Nebraska at Omaha"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Adisu4/cerebral-hemodynamics-aspiration"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of a lumped-parameter model of intracranial
  hemodynamics, cerebrospinal fluid dynamics, and extracranial venous
  drainage, extending the models of Ursino and Lodi and Gadda et al., used to
  simulate flow-controlled aspiration at different sites and flow rates along
  the cerebral venous outflow pathway in post-traumatic intracranial
  hypertension.
keywords:
  - intracranial pressure
  - cerebral venous outflow
  - lumped-parameter model
  - Starling resistor
  - venous aspiration
  - traumatic brain injury
